  "id": "taziyeh_iran",
  "name": "Ta'zieh (Iranian Shi'a passion-play music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Musical passion play of Iranian Shi'a Islam re-enacting the martyrdom of Imam Hossein and his companions at Karbala, staged above all during Muharram in tekyeh arenas and village squares and developed into a great court spectacle under the Qajars. Actors playing the protagonists sing their lines in the modes of Persian classical music while the antagonists declaim theirs, and a small band of long karna trumpets, drums and cymbals signals entrances, battles and turns of the drama; UNESCO has inscribed the Ritual dramatic art of Ta'zīye on its Representative List.",
  "recipe": "classic modern ta'zieh, funeral Lament, middle eastern branch. karna trumpet, dohol, credited cymbals. urban courtyard. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
